WEBVTT

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.380
<i>The </i>Kengan<i> match</i>

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:19.600
<i>can only be watched by selected members</i>
<i>and other authorized people.</i>

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.940
<i>It is held outside of the public eye.</i>

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.860
<i>The particular atmosphere</i>
<i>makes them so enthusiastic</i>

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.740
<i>that a huge amount of money is exchanged</i>
<i>in just a moment.</i>

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.580
The next <i>Kengan </i>match will be
between GANDAI and Nogi Group.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.200
VENUE: UNDERGROUND PARKING LOT
KIMURA SECURITIES BUILDING

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.330
Ohma Tokita,
the affiliated fighter for Nogi Group.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.420
Chairman Nogi
and Ms. Akiyama are late.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.300
The match could begin at any moment.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.630
KAZUO YAMASHITA
NOGI PUBLICATIONS, NOGI GROUP

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.970
Well, I still can't believe it.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.430
Ohma's opponent for today is--

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.060
On the other side is
the affiliated fighter for GANDAI.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:07.850
Jun Sekibayashi!

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.900
<i>Jun Sekibayashi, known as "Hell's Angel,"</i>
<i>from Super Japan Pro-Wrestling,</i>

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:17.860
<i>a major organization covering</i>
<i>every style from hardcore to standard.</i>

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.580
<i>As its unshakable champion,</i>

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:24.710
<i>he is a big name</i>
<i>in public combat sports.</i>

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.920
<i>Public combat sports versus</i>
<i>underground martial arts...</i>

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:32.250
<i>I can't miss such a big match!</i>

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:07.970
THE STRONG

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.600
Stay away from each other.
On your mark, okay?

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.810
Hey, new boy.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.940
I'll tell you something.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:20.990
I'm nothing like the guys you've fought
so far in your <i>Kengan </i>career.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:24.780
I am the first fighter you've faced

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.040
who is an authentic warrior.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:31.040
Are you ready, you two?

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.670
Okay, set.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.090
-Fight!
-Now let's--

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:42.220
You are such a talkative warrior.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:44.260
You're totally unguarded.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.180
Sorry for that.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.020
The nature of my profession
makes me talkative.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:01.650
Nice reflexes.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.620
Arm Whip?
A classic technique.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.200
Ohma's punch didn't hurt him.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.620
He's physically tougher than Lihito.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.960
<i>Yes, you're doing well.</i>

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.260
<i>Although it was such</i>
<i>a strange form of kicking,</i>

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.560
<i>he easily kicked out Ohma</i>
<i>who weighs over 80kg!</i>

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:35.650
<i>This is a professional wrestler.</i>
<i>This is Jun Sekibayashi!</i>

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.110
HIDEKI NOGI,
CHAIRMAN OF NOGI GROUP

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.110
GEN SHIKANO,
CHAIRMAN OF GANDAI

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:46.360
You're doing well.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:48.660
Exercise your right fully.

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.370
Right to what?

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.290
I mean, you guys have a right...

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.790
to escape from pain.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:02.130
By receiving, passing off,
or avoiding the attacks,

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.800
you can use all possible ways
to guard yourself.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:09.640
On the other hand,
we wrestlers have a duty.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:14.060
Whether it's blunt weapons, knives
or even bombs,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.690
professional wrestlers have a duty
to face them head-on.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:22.230
This is your right, and our duty.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:26.530
Now exercise your right
as much as you like.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:28.070
You amateur.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.160
<i>He looks down on</i>
<i>all people except pro-wrestlers.</i>

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.960
<i>He's clearly looking down!</i>

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.670
Do you like close combat?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.930
You rat! What are you doing?

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.300
You've just escaped...

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.050
from pain.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.640
You failed to fulfill your duty.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:57.020
You think you're funny?

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.730
Here it comes! Ohma's...

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.030
Ohma's what?

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.490
A technique... to control
the flow of power!

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:15.790
It's working! Go Ohma!

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.210
Keep on pushing.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.090
Give him a finishing one, Ohma!

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.630
Okay, the bonus time is over.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.010
Just remember.

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:37.060
We professional wrestlers are
great actors, too.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.480
No, Ohma!

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:46.780
<i>That's the first time</i>
<i>I've heard that sound.</i>

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.910
<i>The sound of flesh</i>
<i>being slammed down on the concrete floor.</i>

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.950
Tokita, you okay?

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:56.040
-Can you go on?
-Stand up!

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:02.670
-All right, then! Here I go!
-Sekibayashi!

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:08.590
He pulled him up!

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.180
Once again.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:23.310
Ohma, please!

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.940
Has he... blacked out?

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.990
All right, another one!

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.360
Sekibayashi!

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.490
-Ohma!
-Great, Sekibayashi!

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:39.160
Finish him off!

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.580
You should surrender now, young man!

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:47.130
You can't win,
so just give up before he kills you.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.840
-Take it back!
-Huh?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.140
Take back what you just said.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.470
Who are you?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.310
Ohma never loses.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.600
He will never lose,
even if the opponent is Sekibayashi.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:07.110
"Never loses"?

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.690
But how could he win in that situation?

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.950
Sorry to tell you this,
but there's no chance.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:15.870
You don't understand.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:21.200
Ohma Tokita is a man
who'll never end like this.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:25.040
Whatever kind of monster it is,
he can ultimately beat it.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.880
That's Ohma!

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.590
Sorry to interrupt your speech,
but your friend is about to be ended.

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:37.760
All right. It's almost the time
to finish this match.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:41.680
Dramatically, okay?

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.230
-Yay!
-Oh no!

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:47.400
That's Sekibayashi's killer technique.

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:49.320
Argentine Backbreaker!

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:53.700
No way!

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:55.240
Please.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:58.240
Will you really end here, Ohma?

00:08:58.490 --> 00:08:59.580
Come on!

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.040
For God's sake, please fight back!

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:24.310
When was the last time I came here?

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:34.940
I'll borrow it from you again
for the first time in a while.

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:44.000
What's that sound?

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.500
What the heck is going on?

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:58.470
What... did you do to me?

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:00.640
His... fingers!

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.480
What did I do?

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.610
I’ve borrowed something in advance!

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:15.030
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:17.320
<i>Solid...</i>

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:24.990
Wow, he's pushing.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.460
He's pushing a man who weighs
60kg more than himself with his power.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.290
What strength that guy has!

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.000
No.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.090
That's not him.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:37.380
That's not his usual style.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.090
What on earth happened to him?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:43.220
<i>You jerk.</i>

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.230
<i>It's getting much more fun!</i>

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.950
<i>Ha! I'm quite disadvantaged...</i>

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:06.950
<i>with these fingers.</i>

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.420
<i>But... excellent!</i>

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.460
<i>The harder my challenge is...</i>

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.090
<i>the more excited the audience gets.</i>

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.890
<i>He did a backhand chop</i>
<i>with broken fingers!</i>

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.390
<i>That didn't stop him, huh?</i>

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.230
What's going on in this match?

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:39.280
Tokita punches brutally
and Sekibayashi just withstands it.

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.280
Is it an endurance game?

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.580
Hey, look.

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.410
He's even going forward.

00:11:50.580 --> 00:11:52.830
Being attacked like a typhoon...

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.500
Sekibayashi isn't over yet!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.250
He kicked him back.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:00.050
Neither gives in an inch.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:08.100
<i>No.</i>

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:12.810
<i>It's entirely different from</i>
<i>Ohma's usual fighting style.</i>

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:17.820
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI,
FURUMI PHARMA

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:19.940
What's up, Wakatsuki?

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:22.780
Hey, Imai.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:24.740
Hey. Long time no see.

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:26.700
COSMO IMAI,
NISHIHONJI SECURITY SERVICES

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.200
Well, he's amazing.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.870
His power is no less than
that of Sekibayashi.

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:37.130
That's not about power but rotation rate.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:38.540
Rotation rate?

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:42.340
<i>Right. What increased in him is</i>
<i>not the power but the speed.</i>

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:47.880
<i>With the same mass, his attack naturally</i>
<i>gets stronger according to the speed.</i>

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.310
<i>The faster speed also</i>
<i>tremendously increases</i>

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:53.940
<i>the frequency of punches</i>
<i>compared to before.</i>

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.270
<i>That is the rotation rate.</i>

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:01.360
You guys always think about
such complicated stuff while you fight?

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.700
You think too little.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:09.530
<i>What I want to know is</i>
<i>where this new power came from.</i>

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.660
Anyway, the way Tokita moves is different

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.540
from that in the match with Lihito.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.550
<i>Today's Ohma looks like a savage beast</i>

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:26.300
<i>that shows raw aggressiveness</i>
<i>and demonic character.</i>

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:28.800
<i>I've never seen this side of him.</i>

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.180
<i>Is it Ohma's true identity?</i>

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:39.020
-It's a hit!
-What are you doing, Sekibayashi?

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:42.610
-Defend yourself!
-I bet a lot of money on you!

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.030
<i>They don't understand.</i>

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.700
<i>How could you be a professional wrestler</i>

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.620
<i>without taking all the attacks?</i>

00:13:58.880 --> 00:14:00.210
Come on!

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:10.550
-Sekibayashi is coming back!
-Go!

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:12.600
Hey, what's wrong?

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:15.850
Don't take a rest there.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.520
Okay, I'm going to finish this match.

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:22.980
Sekibayashi!

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.650
-Finish it!
-Ohma, please!

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.740
Here I come!

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.470
What was that?

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:59.390
-That was...
-Yeah.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:02.650
That man cut off his air supply.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:04.690
Finished?

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.360
What just happened?

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:09.860
He beat Sekibayashi with one punch?

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.210
<i>I see!</i>

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.210
<i>He targeted Sekibayashi's windpipe.</i>

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:29.670
<i>Once the air supply to the brain</i>
<i>is cut off,</i>

00:15:30.340 --> 00:15:32.050
<i>his tenacity doesn't matter anymore.</i>

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.100
<i>He couldn't stay conscious.</i>

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:40.140
<i>Ohma's attacking power, combined with</i>
<i>Sekibayashi's rushing power,</i>

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.350
<i>converted entirely into</i>
<i>damage to Sekibayashi.</i>

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:46.940
<i>Ohma was waiting for a chance to counter.</i>

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:49.180
The winner is Ohma Tokita for Nogi Group.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.110
WINNER: OHMA TOKITA (NOGI GROUP)
LOSER: JUN SEKIBAYASHI (GANDAI)

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.320
Yes.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.040
He did it!

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:00.830
<i>I was wrong.</i>

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:03.170
<i>He's not different at all.</i>

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:07.800
<i>As I saw, the primal instinct of fighting</i>
<i>and the sophisticated game plan</i>

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.550
<i>are the true nature of Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.550
You were too hardy.

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:15.600
Old man.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:21.430
Oh gosh, you won. You have an eye.

00:16:21.810 --> 00:16:24.230
Oh, thank you.

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.560
I like you!

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:30.400
-Let's have a drink someday.
-Ah, yes.

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.610
A drink?

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:38.080
Oh, well. Whatever.
I have to take care of Ohma first.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.200
<i>Excellent!</i>

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:45.040
What a surprise!

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:49.880
-Is that the chairman?
-No way.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.340
It was excellent.

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:00.180
Who's that?

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.810
-That's...
-Chairman Katahara!

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:05.900
<i>Katahara?</i>

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.370
<i>I must be dreaming.</i>
<i>Why?</i>

00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:12.750
<i>What is the governor of</i>
<i>Dainippon Bank doing here?!</i>

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:13.950
METSUDO KATAHARA

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:15.530
Why is he...

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:16.990
Just to watch the match?

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:19.780
As he's here, Fang must be here, too...

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:22.750
What do you think, Wakatsuki?

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:24.710
I'm not sure, but...

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.880
The chairman of the Kengan Association
has come.

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:30.800
It's obvious the situation is
out of the ordinary.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.920
Chairman Katahara.

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.840
Hi, Nogi.

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:40.300
I really appreciate
your coming here today.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.390
Nogi.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.560
You found a great fighter.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.890
You agree with me, right?

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:50.940
Don't you, Sekibayashi?

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.440
He's indeed a great fighter.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:57.450
I had no idea I would lose.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:01.330
<i>Shit... it’s surprising that hardly</i>
<i>any damage is left in him.</i>

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:04.450
For now, you're the winner.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.630
Even Sekibayashi approves his ability.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.170
It means he really is someone.

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:14.710
So, did you make a decision?

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:16.550
Shikano.

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:18.340
Yes, sir.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.800
You won, Mr. Nogi.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:22.390
I keep my word.

00:18:22.640 --> 00:18:26.480
We, GANDAI, agree with the resolution
proposed by Nogi Group,

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:31.400
calling for the battle for the chairman's
post of the <i>Kengan </i>Association.

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:38.400
<i>The battle for the chairman's post!</i>

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:45.490
You need 50 affirmative votes to hold
the battle for the chairman's post.

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.620
Now the conditions are satisfied.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.670
Which means...

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:57.260
You qualify for crossing swords with me,
Metsudo Katahara.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.260
<i>So much pressure.</i>

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:05.640
<i>An enormous energy like from a volcano</i>
<i>is blowing out from that thin old man.</i>

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:08.230
<i>With his overwhelming presence,</i>

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:10.980
<i>he is like a supernatural being</i>
<i>in a human shape.</i>

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.900
<i>I can't move an inch.</i>

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:16.980
<i>His outrageously extravagant pressure</i>
<i>is still present.</i>

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:21.570
<i>Or, I should say, it keeps growing,</i>
<i>even if he is over 90 already.</i>

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:23.620
<i>That spooky old man...</i>

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:25.950
I know what I'm doing.

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:30.870
Metsudo Katahara, the 58th chairman
of the<i> Kengan</i> Association.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:33.210
I will make you leave your position.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:37.800
That's a good one.

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:41.550
You really make me excited.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.800
I accept your challenge.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:47.720
I allow you to use anything you have

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:51.230
to beat me and Fang of Metsudo.

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:53.480
<i>Fang of Metsudo...</i>

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:55.820
<i>And Fang of Metsudo himself is...</i>

00:19:56.320 --> 00:19:58.940
<i>not with us now, unfortunately.</i>

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.110
Fang...

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:02.530
It's quite difficult to beat him.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:04.660
What the...

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:07.410
The air is thick with tension.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.750
Excuse me, what is Fang of Metsudo?

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.710
-Don't you know?
-No.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.960
He's the fighter
that Metsudo Katahara has.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.590
They say he's the strongest fighter
of all<i> Kengan </i>history.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:24.470
The strongest!

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:30.890
His record is 157 victories and no losses,
something no one has ever accomplished.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:35.730
<i>Fang...</i>

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.740
Mr. Katahara, please.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:44.200
Well... as of today,

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:48.330
as the chairman
of the <i>Kengan </i>Association,

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.000
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:57.590
I hereby declare the opening
of the <i>Kengan</i> Life-or-Death Tournament.

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:03.090
"Death" means you may die, right?

00:21:03.340 --> 00:21:06.090
Sounds interesting, I want to join it!

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.850
Maybe I should lead my boss on.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:12.680
Of course, we will participate
in the tournament, too.

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.940
I'll count on you, Sekibayashi.

00:21:15.020 --> 00:21:18.150
Really? You've just seen me lose, sir.

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:22.820
Unfortunately, I don't know
any other fighter greater than you.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:26.950
Besides, professional wrestling is
the best of three points, isn't it?

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:30.990
The best of three points?
What classic rule are you talking about?

00:21:32.870 --> 00:21:35.660
I feel raging energy from each of you.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:39.880
Your wish has no value when it's easily
granted just by having it in mind.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:44.380
Something you truly need is
always lying beyond death.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:48.510
Anyone who wishes to take the position
of the Association Chairman is welcome.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:53.060
Send the fighter you think
is the strongest to the tournament!

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.060
It doesn't matter
if he is a martial artist,

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:59.100
a gangster, or even a psycho killer.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:01.610
Defeat my Fang

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:06.740
and grab your real life beyond death.

00:22:07.530 --> 00:22:08.860
<i>A tournament?</i>

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:12.030
<i>That'll work for me.</i>

00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:17.330
<i>That bastard never misses</i>
<i>an exciting event like this.</i>

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:21.340
<i>I'm sure he'll show up.</i>

00:22:22.210 --> 00:22:23.590
<i>Definitely.</i>

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:30.010
<i>I've been waiting for you, asshole.</i>

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:32.220
<i>Get ready for my attack...</i>

00:22:33.140 --> 00:22:35.060
<i>preserved for these ten years.</i>

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.480
<i>A story of a grudge.</i>

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:10.240
<i>A wish for revenge.</i>

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:12.860
<i>Too far to regard him as a longtime enemy.</i>

00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:16.330
<i>Beyond the food chain in the jungle law,</i>

00:24:16.410 --> 00:24:18.120
<i>there is a man waiting for him.</i>

00:24:18.440 --> 00:24:20.070
<i>Next episode: "Reunited"</i>

00:24:20.170 --> 00:24:21.870
Subtitle translation by Hinako Someno
